DesignCraft VAIO preview
Unofficial native i386 build for Ubuntu 16.04 / Atom Z540.

Desktop: designcraft-vaio [FILE.designcraft|FILE.idml]
Headless: designcraft-vaio-cli --help
Example: designcraft-vaio-cli run --in Brochure.designcraft --export Brochure.pdf
MCP: designcraft-vaio-cli mcp --automation-read-root DIR --automation-write-root DIR
GUI control is opt-in (--control PORT), loopback only, without authentication.
Enable it only while needed. Headless MCP supports explicit file-access roots.

Glow presents the interface using the existing software OpenGL driver. Document
rendering remains CPU based. Fonts and original upstream engines are retained.
A steady caret and reduced motion avoid repeated llvmpipe redraws. Set
DESIGNCRAFT_STATIC_CARET=0 for one launch to restore blinking/animation. Recovery
wakes the idle editor on its snapshot schedule (default 30 seconds).
The private libxcb is package-local; system libraries are not replaced.

Suitable for small brochures, flyers and page layouts. Upstream is pre-alpha;
complex external INDD/IDML, professional prepress and large layouts are unverified.
Use explicit pages and manual threading: primary-frame Smart Text Reflow has a
known upstream page-growth issue. Keep native originals and check exported pages.

APT manages installation and updates through the existing Check & Install Updates
frontend. Removal: sudo apt-get remove designcraft-vaio (documents/settings remain).
Preferences/recovery default to ~/.config/designcraft and the upstream recovery
location. DESIGNCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR selects an isolated profile including Recovery.
